  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Monday)\nIssued at 1249 PM CDT TUE SEP 8 2026\n\nThe weather story for most of this forecast period will continue\nto be the persistent upper-level ridging and associated heat.\nAfternoon highs will generally range in the low to mid-90s into\nthe weekend, with heat index values remaining above triple-\ndigits. While we will remain below any heat advisory criteria,\nprolonged outdoor exposure will still easily result in heat\nrelated illness. Thankfully, this ridge should become slightly\ncompressed by Friday, as a deep trough and cold front work\nthrough the Midwest. This cold front will eventually lose the\nbest upper-level support, stalling somewhere along northern\nTennessee, allowing for slightly more organized rain chances\nthrough the weekend.\n\nForecast confidence decreases Monday as the upper-level ridge is\nexpected to rebuild once more by the start of next workweek. Some\nguidance builds the ridge back quickly, while other guidance has\nit return much more slowly. This scenario would allow for some\nlow-end rain chances (<30%) to remain in the forecast through\nthen, but again, confidence here is low. Regardless, it appears\nthat the ridge will return in some capacity, with afternoon highs\nreturning right back into the low to mid-90s.\n\n/44/",
